  "response_text": "Using #include <kernel.c> is a bad idea because .c files should be compiled separately, not pasted into other files. Including a .c file mixes everything into one big file before compiling, which can cause problems like duplicated code or strange errors. Instead, we should use header files (.h) to share function declarations between files. This keeps the code organized and avoids bugs. The compiler is designed to work with .c files on their own, so including them directly breaks the normal build process and makes the project harder to manage.\\n",
